# History: this file briefly suppressed CVE-2026-5773 and CVE-2026-6276
# (curl/libcurl, HIGH) while the fix (curl 8.20.0-r0+) lagged Alpine's
# v3.23 stable branch. Resolved 2026-07-17 by bumping the base image to
# the Alpine 3.24 line (ghcr.io/linuxserver/baseimage-alpine:3.24-03b33b49-ls6),
# which ships curl 8.21.0-r0 and does not need the ignore. See the FROM
# comment in the Dockerfile for the full record.
#
# History (2026-09-08 to 2026-10-29): eight entries here suppressed CVEs
# against pip's OWN vendored copies -- pip/_vendor/msgpack 1.1.2
# (GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964, CVE-2026-114613), pip/_vendor/setuptools 70.3.0
# (CVE-2025-47273, CVE-2026-59890, GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w) and
# pip/_vendor/urllib3 2.7.0 (CVE-2026-97687, CVE-2026-97688, CVE-2026-97689)
# -- because pip shipped in the image even though only the build used it.
# Since 2026-10-29 the Dockerfile installs and uninstalls pip (venv pip and
# Alpine's py3-pip) inside the one layer that needs it and fails the build if
# either is still importable, so no pip, and none of those vendored copies,
# reaches the image. The entries were removed rather than kept "just in
# case": a stale ignore would silently hide a real finding if pip ever came
# back. If one does, fix the Dockerfile instead of re-adding them here.
